# Google Hacking & Google Dorks

This project explores **Google Hacking**, also known as **Google Dorking**, as an OSINT technique used to identify publicly indexed information through advanced search operators.

The project demonstrates how carefully crafted search queries can help discover exposed files, publicly accessible directories, sensitive information, and potentially misconfigured web resources.

The main objective is to understand how search engines can be used during the reconnaissance phase of a security assessment, while identifying potential information exposure risks and documenting findings in a structured and responsible manner.

All activities are conducted for educational purposes and focus on publicly available information, authorized targets, and ethical OSINT practices.
